-- title:
--   Round-six lemma `LRep_rgp`
-- statement:
--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6AIL2`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6A.LRep_rgp {K M w post pre : ℕ} (hK : 0 < K) (hM : 0 < M) (hw : 0 < w) (hp : 0 < post)
--       {L : List α} {φ : ℕ → ℕ → List α} (hL : LRep pre (K * (M * w)) post L φ) :
--       LRep (pre * (M * K)) w post (rgp K M w post pre L)
--         (fun b' c => (((φ (b' / (M * K)) c).drop ((b' % K * M + b' % (M * K) / K) * w)).take w))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** A lines, IL side 2: copies and regrouping of line representations
--
--   * `dupL K L`: `K` copies of `L` concatenated (what the IL duplication leaves on stack `0`);
--   * **`LRep_cpy`**: `K = 2^f` copies of a `(pre, n, post)` array, followed by the two fine
--     exposures `(1, K, N) → (1, N, K)` and `(pre, n·post, K) → (pre, K, n·post)`, are the
--     `(pre, K·n, post)` array whose lines are `K` copies of the old lines;
--   * **`LRep_rgp`**: a `(pre, K·M·w, post)` array (`K = 2^f` classes of `M` windows of length `w`),
--     after the exposures `(pre, K, M·w·post) → (pre, M·w·post, K)` and
--     `(pre·M, w·post, K) → (pre·M, K, w·post)`, is the `(pre·(M·K), w, post)` array whose row
--     `b·(M K) + j K + r` is window `j` of class `r` of line `b`.
--
